# Repo-root ignores. Several services also carry their own .gitignore
# (services/voicehr, services/resume-intelligence, services/recruitment-workflow/frontend);
# those are more specific and stay authoritative inside their own tree. This file covers
# the repo root and any service that does not have one of its own (second-brain,
# recruitment-workflow, benchmarks, infra, tests).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration  -- NEVER commit these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every service reads its own .env (see infra/docker-compose.yml env_file:). They hold
# GEMINI_API_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, the JWT secret and the webhook HMAC secret. Only the
# .env.example templates are tracked.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Candidate data (PII) -- privacy boundary, not just hygiene
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interview audio is the candidate's recorded voice; transcripts are what they said.
# Resumes are raw PII. None of it belongs in git. .gitkeep files are kept so the
# directory structure survives a clean checkout.
storage/**
!storage/**/
!storage/**/.gitkeep
report/
benchmarks/
# Raw resume uploads, wherever they land.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
!docs/**/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node (services/recruitment-workflow/frontend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local databases and model weights
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VoiceHR keeps its own SQLite store; it is per-machine state, never source.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Local LLM weights. Ollama keeps models in ~/.ollama, not here, but a stray GGUF is
# multi-gigabyte and would be painful to remove from history -- so block them at the door.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pt
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, temp files, editors, OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# OneDrive drops desktop.ini into synced folders -- this repo lives in one.
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored -- do not "clean these up"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# benchmarks/local_llm/results/*.json  -- the raw measurements behind
#   LOCAL_LLM_BENCHMARK_AND_FALLBACK.md; the report's numbers are unverifiable without them.
# benchmarks/local_llm/graphs/*.png    -- the 11 figures referenced by the report.
# services/voicehr/tests/benchmark_results/latest.{json,md} -- committed golden-case output.
# Each service's .env.example          -- the template a new checkout copies from.
